<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 December, from 856 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/damghan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damghan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">856 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Damghan earthquake strikes the eastern Alborz mountains</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake of estimated magnitude 7.9 struck near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damghan">Damghan</a>, capital of the province of Qumis in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, with its worst shaking along some 350 kilometres of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a>. It caused approximately 200,000 deaths, though the toll is debated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">880 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,146 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The rebel Huang Chao captures Luoyang, eastern capital of the Tang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao">Huang Chao</a>'s rebel army quickly took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, the eastern capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>. Emperor Xizong then abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a>, and Huang entered the capital and declared himself emperor of a new state of Qi.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xizong-of-tang">Emperor Xizong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1135">1135 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">891 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen of Blois is crowned king of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after Henry I's death, his nephew Stephen was crowned at Westminster despite having sworn to support <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s daughter, the Empress Matilda. The civil war that followed became known as the Anarchy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1216">1216 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">810 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Honorius III confirms the Dominican Order</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the bull Religiosam vitam, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a> gave universal recognition to the Order of Preachers founded by the Castilian priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-dominic">Dominic de Guzmán</a>. Already recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, the order followed the Rule of St Augustine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican Order</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1489">1489 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">537 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Almería submits to the Catholic Monarchs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The port city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>, part of the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> of the Catholic Monarchs, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-i-of-castile">Isabella I of Castile</a>. The last Nasrid ruler, Muhammad XII, surrendered Granada itself in 1492.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-i-of-castile">Isabella I of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1715">1715 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">311 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Old Pretender lands in Scotland, too late</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-francis-edward-stuart">James Francis Edward Stuart</a> landed at Peterhead to lead the Jacobite rising. After the defeat at Preston and the stalemate at Sheriffmuir in November, the cause was failing, and he sailed back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in February.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1894">1894 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">132 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A court martial convicts Captain Alfred Dreyfus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A French military court convicted the Jewish officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus">Alfred Dreyfus</a> of passing secrets to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and sentenced him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> for life. His innocence, and the cover-up, split <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dreyfus-affair">Dreyfus Affair</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1964">1964 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The SR-71 Blackbird makes its first flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lockheed's SR-71 reconnaissance aircraft first flew at Palmdale, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Able to cruise above Mach 3 at about 25,000 metres, it remains the fastest crewed jet-powered aircraft.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 December <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gang-gam-chan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gang-gam-chan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gang Gam-chan</span><span class="tp">948–1031</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roger-ii-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roger II of Sicily</span><span class="tp">1095–1154</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kuroda-yoshitaka"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kuroda-yoshitaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kuroda Yoshitaka</span><span class="tp">1546–1604</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guru-gobind-singh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guru Gobind Singh</span><span class="tp">1666–1708</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-oglethorpe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Oglethorpe</span><span class="tp">1696–1785</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victoriano-huerta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victoriano Huerta</span><span class="tp">1850–1916</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giacomo-puccini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giacomo-puccini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giacomo Puccini</span><span class="tp">1858–1924</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 December <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baha-al-dawla"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baha-al-dawla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baha al-Dawla</span><span class="tp">970–1012</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-de-bethune-duke-of-sully"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilien-de-bethune-duke-of-sully.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilien de Béthune, Duke of Sully</span><span class="tp">1560–1641</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-eliot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-eliot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Eliot</span><span class="tp">1819–1880</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
